                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "14159ce3-4b83-30f2-a1ba-ece30179db56",
                        "entry_id": "723379a1-0853-3427-b97e-1e66971aecd3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Prediction, prophecy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3405b1ed-c86e-419b-ae5c-1f5da90961b1",
                                "sense_id": "14159ce3-4b83-30f2-a1ba-ece30179db56",
                                "text": "Yorick ſcarce ever heard this ſad vaticination of his deſtiny read over to him, but with a tear ſtealing from his eye, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "38821f5c-2749-4c01-a92d-36bbaa64fdbb",
                                "sense_id": "14159ce3-4b83-30f2-a1ba-ece30179db56",
                                "text": "[…]for that honest gentleman, never the most susceptible of extraneous impressions, had just that moment parted from Meg Merrilies, and was too deeply wrapt up in pondering upon her vaticinations, to make any answer to Hazlewood's call."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f8ba8c76-6350-4db7-8a36-1f40782159fe",
                                "sense_id": "14159ce3-4b83-30f2-a1ba-ece30179db56",
                                "text": "Every surmise and vaticination of the mind is entitled to a certain respect, and we learn to prefer imperfect theories, and sentences, which contain glimpses of truth, to digested systems which have no one valuable suggestion."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5a74e638-19d5-442b-badf-51f182261a02",
                                "sense_id": "14159ce3-4b83-30f2-a1ba-ece30179db56",
                                "text": "The anonymous oracle, the author of this pamphlet, is an example of entertaining dullness. He has manufactured a very damp squib; he is a serious man in motley; and practical ideas occasionally drop in among his fantastic vaticinations."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4f32e5b0-f0c9-4fee-a993-54ff3f0d0bd4",
                                "sense_id": "14159ce3-4b83-30f2-a1ba-ece30179db56",
                                "text": "Archer had been wont to smile at these annual vaticinations of his mother's; but this year even he was obliged to acknowledge, as he listened to an enumeration of the changes, that the \"trend\" was visible."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2cfc55ce-1e40-404d-8351-4c201cb8234f",
                                "sense_id": "14159ce3-4b83-30f2-a1ba-ece30179db56",
                                "text": "[…][Nineteen Eighty-Four] breaks all records for gloomy vaticination[…]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
